WEBVTT

00:00.499 --> 00:03.873
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:03.874 --> 00:07.362
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.363 --> 00:10.399
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.400 --> 00:13.477
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.478 --> 00:16.885
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:16.886 --> 00:20.457
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.458 --> 00:22.026
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.027 --> 00:23.894
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:23.895 --> 00:28.653
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:35.346 --> 00:36.746
Good evening. I'm Tom Tucker.

00:36.747 --> 00:38.648
Coming up, why one hello a day

00:38.649 --> 00:40.985
to the receptionist at work
is the magic number.

00:40.986 --> 00:43.989
But first,
pilot strike at Quahog Airport.

00:43.990 --> 00:47.461
Picketing began on Thursday...
Weird day to start a strike...

00:47.462 --> 00:49.598
And both sides appear to be
at an impasse.

00:49.599 --> 00:51.466
So ground control
is telling Major Tom

00:51.467 --> 00:53.269
this could be long one.

00:53.270 --> 00:56.240
Does anyone else
like David Bowie?

00:56.241 --> 00:57.980
Hey, what the hell is
up with this letter?

00:57.981 --> 01:00.217
It says I'm no longer covered
on your health insurance.

01:00.218 --> 01:01.986
Oh, yeah.
They don't cover dogs no more.

01:01.987 --> 01:04.967
You could do COBRA
for $7,300 a month though.

01:04.968 --> 01:06.769
Would that be something
you'd be interested in?

01:06.770 --> 01:08.906
I need that health insurance.
You know I have a hernia.

01:08.907 --> 01:10.075
What if I need surgery?

01:10.076 --> 01:12.211
Well, if you need
insurance that bad,

01:12.212 --> 01:13.713
maybe it's time
for you to go out

01:13.714 --> 01:15.182
and get a job of your own.

01:15.183 --> 01:16.433
This sucks.

01:16.434 --> 01:18.086
How did you
get a hernia?

01:18.087 --> 01:19.420
Actually, I got
it performing

01:19.421 --> 01:21.523
an incredible
act of heroism.

01:24.545 --> 01:25.930
Oh, my God!

01:25.931 --> 01:28.533
Somebody help me! I'm sinking!

01:30.104 --> 01:32.088
Hurry! I can't hold it!

01:32.089 --> 01:35.143
Okay, let me just
unstrap my baby.

01:35.144 --> 01:37.980
Oh! Oh! Oh!
Slipping, slipping. Sorry.

01:41.753 --> 01:42.920
What do we want?

01:42.921 --> 01:44.059
Fair wages!

01:44.060 --> 01:45.224
When do we want it?

01:45.225 --> 01:47.994
Originally now, but it's
been delayed until 9:40

01:47.995 --> 01:49.979
due to weather in Philly!

01:49.980 --> 01:51.652
This is a mess.

01:51.653 --> 01:54.476
Like when Peter rode that
Access Hollywood bus.

03:11.112 --> 03:12.678
Ah, bachelorette party.

03:12.679 --> 03:14.080
Can I fit this in?

03:18.322 --> 03:19.988
Okay, cool. I got time.

03:21.059 --> 03:22.392
Hello, ladies.

03:22.393 --> 03:24.095
Wow, here comes
the bride, huh?

03:24.096 --> 03:26.298
More than once, if I have
anything to do with it.

03:26.299 --> 03:28.244
Finally, the stripper's here!

03:28.245 --> 03:30.771
What? No, I'm not a stripper.
I'm a pilot.

03:32.307 --> 03:33.975
See? This is a real uniform.

03:33.976 --> 03:36.546
Ooh. Take something
else off, sexy.

03:36.547 --> 03:37.763
Oh, yeah!

03:37.764 --> 03:39.216
All right!

03:40.252 --> 03:41.769
Oh, yeah?

03:41.770 --> 03:43.322
You want a little more, huh?

03:46.928 --> 03:48.663
Yeah! All right.

03:48.664 --> 03:51.099
Who wants me to stow my bag
under their seat?

03:56.508 --> 04:00.445
Boy, and I thought the Federal
Hill bakery had nice buns.

04:01.748 --> 04:03.650
You're talented, Denise.

04:03.651 --> 04:05.786
You should
really go for it.

04:09.193 --> 04:11.011
Wow.

04:11.012 --> 04:13.197
What... a... day.

04:13.198 --> 04:14.432
Please don't comment.

04:14.433 --> 04:15.667
Oh, look at you.

04:15.668 --> 04:17.135
- Did you get a job?
- Bitch.

04:17.136 --> 04:18.538
Did I get a job?

04:18.539 --> 04:21.108
Um, this ain't a life-vest,
sista.

04:21.109 --> 04:24.379
It's a work vest from a little
place called Mega Hardware.

04:24.380 --> 04:26.349
'Cause that's basically
what I am now.

04:26.350 --> 04:29.052
Just an everyday,
working-class Joe.

04:29.053 --> 04:31.856
Well, good for you.

04:31.857 --> 04:33.492
No. No, Brian.

04:33.493 --> 04:35.477
This doesn't
feel right today.

04:35.478 --> 04:36.796
Yes.

04:36.797 --> 04:38.349
There's a rat trap
in that cabinet.

04:38.350 --> 04:40.034
With a foot in it.

04:40.035 --> 04:42.321
And somewhere in this house,
there's a footless rat.

04:42.322 --> 04:44.507
Well, I'm off to
watch some Fox News

04:44.508 --> 04:46.243
in front of the
old boob tube.

04:46.244 --> 04:48.546
♪ Tommy used to
work on the docks ♪

04:48.547 --> 04:49.881
♪ Union's been on strike ♪

04:49.882 --> 04:51.384
♪ He's down on his luck ♪

04:51.385 --> 04:53.562
♪ It's tough, so tough. ♪

04:58.662 --> 04:59.862
- Hey.
- No.

04:59.863 --> 05:00.897
- I wasn't sure.
- I'm sure.

05:00.898 --> 05:02.332
- Okay.
- Well, got to go.

05:02.333 --> 05:03.834
Got to do
some more picketing.

05:03.835 --> 05:06.071
Seriously? It's,
like, 9:00 at night.

05:06.072 --> 05:08.835
Yeah, uh...
well, it's, uh...

05:08.836 --> 05:10.819
Cleveland's stealing
shot glasses!

05:11.686 --> 05:14.612
I don't like drinking NyQuil
out of them little cups.

05:19.791 --> 05:21.426
Where the hell's
Quagmire going?

05:21.427 --> 05:23.061
The airport's that way.

05:23.062 --> 05:24.496
He doesn't know we're
following him, Joe.

05:24.497 --> 05:25.848
You don't have
to duck down.

05:25.849 --> 05:28.368
I'm not. You took a pretty hard
right turn back there.

05:28.369 --> 05:30.472
I've been like this for a while.

05:37.750 --> 05:38.733
What's he doing?

05:38.734 --> 05:40.085
This is one of them places

05:40.086 --> 05:42.288
where women go
to see male strippers.

05:42.289 --> 05:44.291
Some bisexual men
go as well.

05:50.000 --> 05:51.479
I don't see him.

05:55.341 --> 05:57.309
Ladies,
this is your pilot speaking.

05:57.310 --> 06:00.947
I am in the full, upright
and locked position.

06:07.591 --> 06:09.092
Oh, my.

06:24.014 --> 06:26.115
Oh, my God!
What are you guys doing here?!

06:26.116 --> 06:27.951
Crap. Our
disguises didn't work.

06:30.590 --> 06:33.025
Quagmire, I didn't know
you were a male stripper.

06:33.026 --> 06:35.462
I wasn't. Not until
the strike, anyway.

06:35.463 --> 06:37.031
I've been out of work
for three weeks.

06:37.032 --> 06:39.134
I'm out of money.
I-I had to do something.

06:39.135 --> 06:40.969
God, I'm so embarrassed.

06:40.970 --> 06:43.649
Why? Stripping is
a very respectable profession.

06:43.650 --> 06:44.742
If it weren't respectable,

06:44.743 --> 06:47.245
why would real estate agents
go to strip clubs for lunch?

06:47.246 --> 06:49.148
He's right.
This is tremendous.

06:49.149 --> 06:50.800
Are you banging
all these chicks?

06:50.801 --> 06:52.886
Hey, hey!
That is offensive.

06:52.887 --> 06:54.823
I am a dancer,
not a gigolo!

06:54.824 --> 06:57.993
Captain Cockpit, my friend
is about to get married,

06:57.994 --> 07:01.532
and we were wondering if you'd
have sex with her for $500.

07:03.369 --> 07:05.170
I'm a gigolo.

07:05.171 --> 07:06.706
Oh, hey, it's that guy.

07:06.707 --> 07:09.193
Are you gonna say,
"Who else but Quagmire?"

07:09.194 --> 07:11.445
N... uh, no, I, uh, uh,

07:11.446 --> 07:13.615
w-wanted to
know if Quagmire

07:13.616 --> 07:15.368
was available
tomorrow evening?

07:15.369 --> 07:17.054
Are... are you gay?

07:17.055 --> 07:18.455
Uh, of course not. No.

07:18.456 --> 07:21.259
Uh, but I'm
unable to properly

07:21.260 --> 07:24.948
have sex with my wife,
so I figured, you know.

07:24.949 --> 07:27.401
Eh, who else
but Quagmire?

07:27.402 --> 07:29.657
Hey, awesome cameo.

07:34.568 --> 07:35.834
Hey, sorry I'm late, guys.

07:35.835 --> 07:37.237
Had to stop at
the dry cleaner.

07:37.238 --> 07:38.471
The dry cleaner?

07:38.472 --> 07:40.040
Wow, somebody
struck it rich.

07:40.041 --> 07:41.509
You know,
I got to tell you,

07:41.510 --> 07:43.144
I was sweating
that pilot strike,

07:43.145 --> 07:46.165
but now that I'm a gigolo,
I'm making money by the fistful.

07:46.166 --> 07:47.534
Is that a giggity?

07:47.535 --> 07:49.052
That is a giggity.

07:49.053 --> 07:50.688
Hey, Quagmire, I
couldn't help but notice

07:50.689 --> 07:52.191
