15:02.813 --> 15:04.247
But I like your effort, Luis.

15:04.248 --> 15:05.499
Uh, any other ideas?

15:05.500 --> 15:06.818
You could kill a guy.

15:06.819 --> 15:09.321
You know what, Carlos,
you stay quiet for a while.

15:09.322 --> 15:10.756
I really only
need two of you.

15:10.757 --> 15:11.825
You'll still be paid.

15:11.826 --> 15:13.726
You ask for papers?

15:13.727 --> 15:16.397
Okay, is there any idea out
there besides killing a guy

15:16.398 --> 15:17.833
or getting
someone deported?

15:17.834 --> 15:19.836
We do good job,
we live with you?

15:19.837 --> 15:21.705
Well, you just
offered to kill a guy,

15:21.706 --> 15:24.024
so you're not exactly number
one on my roommate list.

15:24.025 --> 15:26.678
Now, let's go. I paid good
money for you, I need answers!

15:26.679 --> 15:28.681
I want your best,
and I won't stand for

15:28.682 --> 15:30.176
even one more
stupid idea!

15:31.052 --> 15:33.871
You shake up boss's soda
and give to him.

15:33.872 --> 15:36.253
When he open it,
it explode!

15:37.736 --> 15:39.963
This is why
I pushed you.

15:45.139 --> 15:48.408
Huh. I guess that Brian Griffin
is a good egg after all.

15:50.429 --> 15:52.504
Griffin, you're fired!

16:02.297 --> 16:04.330
I never liked prostitutes

16:04.331 --> 16:07.886
because they sell their bodies
to all types of men.

16:07.887 --> 16:09.572
I turned my first trick

16:09.573 --> 16:11.874
when I had my first
one-night stand.

16:11.875 --> 16:14.779
I had sex for
dinner and drinks.

16:14.780 --> 16:17.082
Being a prostitute is no fun.

16:17.083 --> 16:19.819
You have to work nights,
weekends.

16:19.820 --> 16:22.473
I hear on SNL the women are
funnier than the guys now,

16:22.474 --> 16:24.159
but I don't know,
I'll never see it.

16:29.167 --> 16:30.634
We meet Quagmire,

16:30.635 --> 16:32.837
a small-town boy
with big-city dreams

16:32.838 --> 16:35.608
who has fallen deep
into the game of prostitution

16:35.609 --> 16:36.876
at the Point.

16:38.947 --> 16:40.498
You know, some people ask me,

16:40.499 --> 16:42.751
"Would you want your son
to be a hooker?"

16:42.752 --> 16:44.721
My answer is always,
"Hey, lady, are we talking,

16:44.722 --> 16:45.956
or am I beefing ya?"

16:48.060 --> 16:50.362
I kind of want to see
Guardians of the Galaxy,

16:50.363 --> 16:53.206
but I also kind of feel like
there might be scary parts.

16:54.433 --> 16:56.586
Hey, honey,
you shopping for groceries?

16:57.032 --> 16:58.206
You know what that means?

16:58.207 --> 17:00.076
"Shopping for groceries"
is what I say instead of,

17:00.077 --> 17:01.727
"Do you want to
pay me for sex?"

17:01.728 --> 17:03.245
so I can't get arrested.

17:23.250 --> 17:25.111
Stewie, did you hire
three Mexican guys

17:25.112 --> 17:27.447
to shake a soda can
and give it to my boss?

17:27.448 --> 17:28.832
What?!

17:28.833 --> 17:30.068
One's Guatemalan.

17:30.069 --> 17:31.719
Damn it, Stewie,
you got me fired!

17:31.720 --> 17:33.706
Oh, who are you kidding?
You got yourself fired.

17:33.707 --> 17:35.025
Parading around there,

17:35.026 --> 17:36.726
pretending you know
the first thing about tools.

17:36.727 --> 17:37.607
You know what?

17:37.608 --> 17:39.463
You're going down there
with me right now

17:39.464 --> 17:40.799
to tell them what you did.

17:40.800 --> 17:41.950
Get your hands off me!

17:41.951 --> 17:43.770
I'll go floppy
dead weight on you!

17:46.241 --> 17:47.742
Ah, crap! My stomach!

17:47.743 --> 17:49.094
I think my hernia ruptured!

17:49.095 --> 17:50.279
Oh, my God!

17:50.280 --> 17:52.214
Damn it, it's bad. It's bad!

17:52.215 --> 17:54.084
I'll get Lois. She can take you
to the hospital.

17:54.085 --> 17:55.486
No, she can't.

17:55.487 --> 17:57.322
Thanks to you,
I don't have insurance anymore.

17:57.323 --> 17:58.424
What are we gonna do?!

17:58.425 --> 17:59.725
I'll get the gun!

17:59.726 --> 18:01.661
No, Stewie, you
have to fix me.

18:01.662 --> 18:03.297
What?! I'm not a doctor!

18:03.298 --> 18:05.067
Just look it up
on your phone or something!

18:05.068 --> 18:07.837
Ugh, hold on.
I've got to update iOS.

18:07.838 --> 18:08.905
Stewie!

18:08.906 --> 18:10.507
Okay, okay, got it.

18:10.508 --> 18:12.176
It says I have to make
an incision,

18:12.177 --> 18:13.778
retract the hernia sac,

18:13.779 --> 18:15.815
and then suture
the abdominal lining.

18:15.816 --> 18:17.149
How am I supposed to do that?!

18:17.150 --> 18:18.585
Grab my tool belt.

18:18.586 --> 18:21.139
Use the self-sharpening
linoleum blade.

18:21.140 --> 18:23.942
Ah!

18:23.943 --> 18:26.763
And then hold the incision open
with a vise grip,

18:26.764 --> 18:30.167
and use the slip-joint pliers to
get the muscle back in position.

18:30.168 --> 18:31.503
Okay, okay.

18:31.504 --> 18:33.206
Now it's saying
I have to suture it.

18:33.207 --> 18:35.376
I've got some monofilament line
you can use.

18:35.377 --> 18:37.779
It's from aisle eight,
above the chains and cables.

18:37.780 --> 18:40.115
"Monofilament line,"
"slip-joint pliers."

18:40.116 --> 18:42.651
I've got to say, Brian,
it seems like you really did

18:42.652 --> 18:43.987
learn something on that job.

18:43.988 --> 18:46.557
You're right. I guess I did.

18:46.558 --> 18:47.960
But please, stitch me up.

18:47.961 --> 18:49.561
Just be careful
and take your time.

18:49.562 --> 18:51.030
This is the delicate part,
because...

18:51.031 --> 18:52.833
Yeah, I'm gonna
just use the staple gun.

18:52.834 --> 18:55.136
Ah! Damn it! Ah!

18:55.137 --> 18:57.038
You know what?
That was really easy.

18:57.039 --> 19:00.242
That guy who killed Joan Rivers
must be terrible at this.

19:04.851 --> 19:07.253
Hey, there... Oh.
What are you doing here?

19:07.254 --> 19:08.388
Quagmire?

19:08.389 --> 19:09.756
Uh, oh... uh, uh...

19:09.757 --> 19:12.160
I have a hobby that
takes me this way.

19:12.161 --> 19:14.363
Hey, I'm freezing. You got
a blanket in there or something?

19:14.364 --> 19:17.934
I got a towel, but it's wet
because I'm eating peaches.

19:17.935 --> 19:19.587
I lied about the hobby.

19:19.588 --> 19:21.106
I was sinning.

19:21.107 --> 19:23.722
I'm going to drive
away backwards now.

19:28.785 --> 19:30.235
Hey, baby,
you want to party?

19:30.236 --> 19:31.621
Get in.

19:38.398 --> 19:39.928
You guys having
a good night?

19:41.035 --> 19:42.782
I like that it's
getting dark earlier.

19:43.238 --> 19:45.406
What are you guys
gonna be for Halloween?

19:45.407 --> 19:46.441
Big Pete, help!

19:46.442 --> 19:48.211
She wants to do German things!

19:48.212 --> 19:49.762
German things!

19:49.763 --> 19:52.082
What? No! He hasn't eaten
anything in days!

19:52.083 --> 19:53.585
It's not gonna work!

19:53.586 --> 19:55.921
Nein! Nein!

19:58.826 --> 20:00.494
Ah! She's got us both!

20:00.495 --> 20:02.096
Help us, pimps and hos!

20:02.097 --> 20:05.001
Help us, HBO camera crew!

20:08.974 --> 20:12.177
God, Quagmire, most of
that was horrible.

20:12.178 --> 20:13.496
I know.

20:13.497 --> 20:15.331
Eventually, I might
want to try it again.

20:15.332 --> 20:16.583
Hey, listen, buddy.

20:16.584 --> 20:18.463
I'm sorry
about all this.

20:18.464 --> 20:20.288
I guess I just got
caught up in the money

20:20.289 --> 20:22.191
and-and assumed you
were okay with it

20:22.192 --> 20:23.693
because of the sex.

20:23.694 --> 20:25.295
I don't know, Peter.
I think you're just mad

20:25.296 --> 20:27.431
I didn't come to see
your Pretenders cover band.

20:27.432 --> 20:28.834
Yes, well, that may be.

20:28.835 --> 20:30.836
Speaking of which,
the Pretend Pretenders

20:30.837 --> 20:32.472
are playing again
this weekend.

20:32.473 --> 20:33.841
Uh, much like
the real band,

20:33.842 --> 20:36.294
we have been
described as "meh."

20:36.295 --> 20:38.163
Still, I'm really sorry.

20:38.164 --> 20:40.149
Can you find it in
yourself to forgive me,

20:40.150 --> 20:42.502
and maybe we can just
go back to being friends?

20:42.503 --> 20:44.289
I'd like that.

20:44.290 --> 20:45.723
Hopefully, the pilot strike
will end soon

20:45.724 --> 20:47.276
and I can get my old job back.

20:47.277 --> 20:48.795
Oh, the strike
ended a month ago.

20:48.796 --> 20:50.488
What?!
Why didn't you tell me?!

20:50.489 --> 20:51.515
I did.

20:51.516 --> 20:54.772
Are you still
GlennQ10@aol.com?

20:54.773 --> 20:55.471
No.

20:55.472 --> 20:57.233
Ah, well. There you go.

20:57.234 --> 20:59.235
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru